ed}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305731} :answer-field/id #uuid "034e9426-2cb9-545f-a8bf-8151560f1dcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e83b1a2-7579-5dd1-bddd-671f2c156572" :question/math-academy-id "q-334330" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note: