ype {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property of equality" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396925} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c455c64-6a5a-53e9-8592-0cd96bbb254d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396922} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3dfad07-3750-584e-9f6f-d30755695967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396928} {:answer/id #uuid "995b3536-4529-5769-9f9a-f34c8177e004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying $Φ(t)$ with it's inverse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396929} {:answer/id #uuid "dd384e88-52b2-55f6-8382-7ee54663a081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396930} {:answer/id #uuid "83c3e129-5f38-5e53-b0a2-61bbd06b2d41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83c3e129-5f38-5e53-b0a2-61bbd06b2d41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396931} :answer-field/id #uuid "f108e315-8611-579e-a41e-01f211239093" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396927} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "638ac533-2df7-530f-9f02-d6db96ca8dd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396933} {:answer/id #uuid "fe02d4db-11ef-5015-aea5-bf6b6e4b9f87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396934} {:answer/id #uuid "1a1b6e19-58ed-5e2e-97f8-48746da9e753" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "638ac533-2df7-530f-9f02-d6db96ca8dd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396933} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe7c7b3b-bbe4-57bb-8ae1-e9580b65ffd9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fcd6208-dde9-5e8a-b2c1-ff9f0dade0db" :question/math-academy-id "q-336107" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that every solution $x(t)$ can be written in the form $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c=[{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}]^{T}$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of solutions\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)$ can be written as $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)\\,c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from {{field-1}} by the definition of a fundamental matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines {{field-3}} by {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the definition of a fundamental matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are the columns of $Φ(t),$ we can write\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen by the definition of matrix multiplication,\n\n$$\nΦ(t)\\,c=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of matrix multiplication}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ In $\\text{L3}$ we have $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t),$ and in $\\text{L4}$ we have $Φ(t)c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).$ Since both expressions are equal to the same quantity, the transitive property of equality gives $x(t)=Φ(t)c.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L3 and L4}$ by the $\\text{the transitive property of equality}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "019f61ec-0715-5cf3-adfc-318205b19d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308757} {:answer/id #uuid "1372a77a-5f40-583a-81b0-59907e180c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308888} {:answer/id #uuid "163f0f70-1745-5d82-a520-ee8ffbaf2c9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308914} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb04a3e-77b8-5a44-b01c-eef493e8d810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is diagonalizable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "019f61ec-0715-5cf3-adfc-318205b19d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308757} :answer-field/id #uuid "00d126dd-5882-5b53-ae52-aec393914e29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310795} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ccc770b-7d17-5822-a092-2b7e33126ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating again" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309332} {:answer/id #uuid "98050690-74a9-5e29-9fad-e82f13325cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "factoring out $A$ on the left" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309969} {:answer/id #uuid "9a4cdbf2-f24b-58f9-8cfd-d3356bc5f95f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ(t)$ to both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309991} {:answer/id #uuid "b6ec6680-ddc0-56bc-910c-473286d87036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "transposing the matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98050690-74a9-5e29-9fad-e82f13325cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "factoring out $A$ on the left" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309969} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b0ab1fe-753e-5cd2-bbcb-1248fc35e2e6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49d83357-e4a2-5f75-8ee8-f3623c8527eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "factoring out $A$ on the left" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309313} {:answer/id #uuid "67841cdb-972b-5cb7-9bb7-688577178568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by $A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309540} {:answer/id #uuid "7ec3cfef-16a5-57b7-827e-8492ef849f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating each column" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309737} {:answer/id #uuid "fc81265a-046c-5d73-8138-ffc0ba4f84ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "transposing the matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ec3cfef-16a5-57b7-827e-8492ef849f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating each column" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309737} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab49378a-bc07-5ec8-aa5b-7fade32fbd2c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "72f5b665-78cb-51a0-bf20-214a07f61466" :question/math-academy-id "q-336309" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ satisfies the matrix differential equation ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A\\,Φ(t)$ is given below.\n\n*Hint: $[a,\\,b]$ denotes a matrix whose columns are vectors $a$ and $b.$*\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from the fact that $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix and line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions of the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ Line $\\text{L1}$ identifies ${x}_{2}(t)$ as a column of $Φ(t),$ so ${x}_{2}(t)$ must satisfy the differential equation. In particular,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from the fact that $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix and line $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)],$ the derivative of $Φ(t)$ is obtained by differentiating each column:\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)].\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating each column}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ We now factor the matrix $A$ on the left:\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{factoring out }A\\text{ on the left}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221421 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01bc519d-9d8a-5a50-9ddd-0576fdcea192" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is diagonalizable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442483} {:answer/id #uuid "4fee71ee-9bfc-53d1-9720-277b632cbc77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442506} {:answer/id #uuid "99dac2c2-2f9a-5177-aec9-2c19611bdcf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating each column" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442519} {:answer/id #uuid "e802edfb-19c6-540a-a7d5-687f645229b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e802edfb-19c6-540a-a7d5-687f645229b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442531} :answer-field/id #uuid "2028cfb9-9d36-500c-b53c-d5c401100c51" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442540} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ad643c3-58b8-599d-80d5-1120b49cec66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442500} {:answer/id #uuid "97e4fa85-19f4-5d72-a2e5-d206dea9dd14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442518} {:answer/id #uuid "c1306f31-3a02-5b1e-8df0-d8052ca6d7e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442527} {:answer/id #uuid "fed7e9c9-709f-5270-9ace-aa401742d738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97e4fa85-19f4-5d72-a2e5-d206dea9dd14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442518} :answer-field/id #uuid "95dff24a-69a1-5c42-aa00-bca2089747a2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442548} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02322a89-1398-5bad-8e30-a0a0a268214d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "transposing the matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442484} {:answer/id #uuid "14fbbddb-48b0-5865-92fb-6528fd13c65e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by $A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442490} {:answer/id #uuid "afe05a9e-d5c2-5aa1-9814-2d2e80429809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating each column" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442522} {:answer/id #uuid "d4336788-b670-5b22-9efc-4971c7505f31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ(t)$ to both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afe05a9e-d5c2-5aa1-9814-2d2e80429809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating each column" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442522} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8ae518a-9958-5b32-a5fd-7a9d3da57763" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "df1d5701-ba5a-54b3-9982-7187c6baef60" :question/math-academy-id "q-336312" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ satisfies the matrix differential equation ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A\\,Φ(t)$ is given below.\n\n*Hint: $[a,\\,b]$ denotes a matrix whose columns are vectors $a$ and $b.$*\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix and line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ and substitution from line {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)],$ the derivative of $Φ(t)$ is obtained by differentiating each column:\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)].\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating each column}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its \ncolumns are linearly independent solutions of the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ Line $\\text{L1}$ identifies ${x}_{1}(t)$ as a column of $Φ(t),$ so ${x}_{1}(t)$ must satisfy the differential equation. In particular,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix and $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ From $\\text{L6}$ we have ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)].$ Using $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$ from $\\text{L1},$ we substitute to obtain ${Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t).$ Thus, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by substitution from $\\text{L1}.$"}]}
